didn't blow me away but I've had much worse at much \"nicer\" places. It's Italian classics at a fair price and a generous portion. We started with some appetizers - caprese and calamari that were fun to share. I had the chicken parmigi..."},{"business_id":"UR9dzGGVfcJhHt_mG3bTRA","review_id":"NSdzv77gBkfpTPNRWylx9w","date":"2015-06-09T19:15:17","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9430000185966492,"text_excerpt":"This was honestly one of my favorite dining experiences ever (and I've traveled to a lot of places and eaten at a lot of restaurants). SERVICE Absolutely impeccable, but also friendly and non-pretentious. Our server always had a smile on her face, a great suggestion for food, and the willingness to chat with us. FOOD The meal I had here was one of my favorite entrees I'd ever eaten, but it was also a special that night, so I'm not sure you can always get it: beef cheek over a goat cheese and cauliflower puree. I can't even relay in words how tender and flavorful this meat was. WINE This place doubles as a wine shop, so there's no wine menu per se. You can just walk around and browse the s..."},{"business_id":"UR9dzGGVfcJhHt_mG3bTRA","review_id":"0H6xOtNUaIAn_YHkeiOKfA","date":"2019-01-05T01:50:24","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9410584568977356,"text_excerpt":"One of the best meals that I've had in a long time. I have wanted to try this restaurant for at least a year now. Today was finally the day. The ambience of this place is really nice and cozy. One of my favorite things about it is that you can choose your own bottle of wine. After walking around for several minutes, my husband and I decided on a Spanish wine named Pi (3.14). It was really good. After a little deliberation, I decided on the marsala pork cheeks and my husband ordered seafood Tritone. We also had the calamari for an appetizer and of course tiramisu for dessert. Let me just tell you, those pork cheeks were nicely braised and oh so tender. I didn't hear any complaints about th..."